  "description": "MINKON crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H78 N12 O36 Tb6,3(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.748-3.760 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 108.80-111.37°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C42H84N15O36Tb6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
